explanation:
```js
db.products.updateOne({ _id: pid }, {
  $push: { recentReviews: { $each: [review], $position: 0, $slice: 10 } }
})
```
The cost: two writes per review, and edits or deletes must also update the embedded copy if it's in the subset.

```js
db.createCollection("productViews", {
  timeseries: { timeField: "at", metaField: "productId", granularity: "minutes" }
})
```
Hand-rolled buckets still make sense when you need custom per-bucket fields or update semantics that time series collections don't fit.
